troke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R1lj2:"><div data-rid="c9e6869c-05a4-4836-86b9-6b6657e4cfa9" class="r-1t6dw6g"><div data-rid="eca399a5-0280-49d1-a555-50a4a05d13a0" class="r-1yg88pr alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Monthlies is a premium supplement that combines natural ingredients to support your menstrual cycle. You simply add one scoop to water once a day.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="37c65091-81f0-4175-a73f-38c10c293c68" class="r-1a60wti" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="b7593214-e9bc-4aef-95c2-130f70c8e1ba" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R2lj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-94qlny"><div data-rid="d5cb9b9f-e999-4399-b859-4d49cd956f09" class="r-1ynpu11 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What does monthlies taste like?</p></span></div><div data-rid="e1289fb1-2416-4972-80e8-fdd46a43b23e" class="r-7jypz3"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R2lj2:"><div data-rid="90615d37-4c9b-43e9-8019-43414e88cf89" class="r-1g8lly7"><div data-rid="14f121c8-9b65-4d14-9610-3320722cc5db" class="r-7dstf4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies has a tropical, slightly gingery taste. If it's a bit strong for you, you can try mixing it with more water and sipping it slowly. You can also add it to a smoothie or blend it into a cold beverage to make it easier and more enjoyable to take daily.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="9d6dfa5a-6304-4b1e-932d-82b3eb6d7242" class="r-1y94181" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="f53d9f0a-f9ac-4272-bc19-7445f88ac5a4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R3lj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-dik73z"><div data-rid="675081e2-ef59-43d2-a891-f46ea44508aa" class="r-9kmqok alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I'm using hormonal contraceptive?</p></span></div><div data-rid="554d3b35-7177-400c-bd89-c8741b21382e" class="r-1jmrff1"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R3lj2:"><div data-rid="8b42f868-7e89-457e-bb5a-26ff127553bc" class="r-2vsgxo"><div data-rid="729442d2-1686-4cc5-84a8-303e6d8fc573" class="r-rdofpc alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>You can take monthlies while on birth control or hormonal contraceptive pills; however, it's essential to understand that the effectiveness of monthlies may vary since your hormones are already being regulated. Additionally, monthlies could potentially interact with your hormonal birth control. To ensure safety, it's always best to consult your doctor before adding any new supplements to your routine. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="f7283662-e790-447d-86dc-37ca7986cc73" class="r-1rpu8tr" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="babe7f62-de69-454a-a79f-249718286440" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R4lj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-m1thgk"><div data-rid="cb0a7ebe-78ed-439e-a11b-78c7d668f158" class="r-1i8qo9 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Is monthlies suitable for a teenager?</p></span></div><div data-rid="20f9f831-c87b-4cca-a2ac-79e21eb4459a" class="r-1v2hp2a"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R4lj2:"><div data-rid="3b265b66-e7ba-4d87-8eaf-9b83c1a3a531" class="r-1f16dev"><div data-rid="0aac3d86-0d97-4190-a56a-2bf4bc8f76ff" class="r-tx93jw alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies is recommended for females above the age of 16, as this is when their menstrual cycle and hormonal system usually begins to stabilise. For teenagers under the age of 16 (18 in Germany), we suggest consulting a doctor before introducing any new supplement. While monthlies is formulated with science-backed vitamins, minerals and plant extracts that support menstrual health, it's always best to get individual advice for the teen's unique needs. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="3bd2f04f-9636-488d-a3e4-b29da809dbaf" class="r-16kv8dr" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="580644cf-a768-4fed-bd89-90a57e0e78c2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R5lj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1ebzqeb"><div data-rid="aa2f37f2-33e9-4aa9-8511-26825ba4cd34" class="r-dknj65 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have endometriosis?</p></span></div><div data-rid="3f9c9115-0c13-4f12-b2f5-e198978b54f2" class="r-1cdmxfy"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R5lj2:"><div data-rid="1d6729e0-407f-4e3a-b609-58c1a8e81c2e" class="r-1gvx8zy"><div data-rid="3b7b5b03-4d70-418e-af79-3a9caa9b93e8" class="r-fbst2e alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have endometriosis. While monthlies is not a treatment for endometriosis, it's designed to support menstrual well-being by addressing some of the underlying triggers of period pain, such a hormonal imbalances, prostaglandin overproduction and nutrient gaps. However, we always recommend you to check with your doctors before adding any new supplements to your routine and check for possible interactions with medications. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="1936a0b8-2bd2-41f1-8c50-43b0eba8f8da" class="r-ye4bjm" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="5798149a-dc28-4d51-a57b-08856dee7db2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R6lj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1tj210r"><div data-rid="00dc735f-f64a-4749-b1c2-cd969fe02361" class="r-8gsuv alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have IBS?</p></span></div><div data-rid="72387ced-4a45-48f8-85d6-a5598bc544bc" class="r-16sgohm"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R6lj2:"><div data-rid="d21684fa-ba88-42fb-a8a4-d8aac21f033b" class="r-d0d5i"><div data-rid="fb67186b-2dc8-4800-869f-c219a0c38c4f" class="r-w5u7ic alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies can be taken by those with IBS, but since IBS can involve sensitivities to certain ingredients, we recommend reviewing our full ingredient list before introducing it to your routine. If you're unsure about how your body might react, especially to certain dosages and ingredients, it's best to speak to your doctor or a health care professional who understands your condition. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="225fc239-dd84-4675-b856-bc1f99552a5d" class="r-1iws0ma" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="73e98c72-19c7-4e3b-b7ff-b24b5c1387c4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R7lj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1r1ekqr"><div data-rid="623f25f2-3d2d-459b-a531-ecd5975f7c9e" class="r-1uhor1 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have PCOS?</p></span></div><div data-rid="6b5790e0-d97a-465d-99e0-88b0e28df692" class="r-k2kvrg"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R7lj2:"><div data-rid="b46a835a-3dd6-4137-b40d-038014d6e6f8" class="r-mx8z82"><div data-rid="3626b161-dcc4-453f-969b-8856ba0f99e7" class="r-zqzlkz alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have PCOS, as there are many ingredients that may benefit those with PCOS.</p><br><p>However, monthlies is not meant to treat any medical condition so you should always check with your doctor before incorporating new supplements into your routine. Please also check possible interactions with your medications (if any). </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="040554ed-38b3-4b4c-830c-e9d249234857" class="r-3v1o0z" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="61ed0c54-a9b2-44dc-a3ee-a252a115b917" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R8lj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-79iaty"><div data-rid="15b2c69f-765b-401c-ba1f-93c80c279246" class="r-9dltjj alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I am breastfeeding or pregnant?</p></span></div><div data-rid="9855a5e1-b185-47a4-861a-3cf595b77335" class="r-11qfjk8"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R8lj2:"><div data-rid="2364669c-4122-4146-90e6-a597f808717a" class="r-bc5elo"><div data-rid="2ebd1c89-02f2-4123-ab00-f8b278374a41" class="r-1jaldk4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>It is not recommended to take monthlies if you are breastfeeding or pregnant.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="1d620bab-854e-427b-bc38-b6cfc960d1ac" class="r-8v9mac" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="d7fcb280-b80f-40b8-8ad1-bdfae0c636ba" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R9lj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1go4o29"><div data-rid="cbae59ee-1cc3-410f-8185-be78388500a6" class="r-tzjoxx alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How can I book my free consultation?</p></span></div><div data-rid="e3262735-ca8b-4151-af2a-00abb0351c1d" class="r-4olxto"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R9lj2:"><div data-rid="916625e9-38af-407c-b1a7-856c934768c1" class="r-1pq8n43"><div data-rid="e58521fe-7ba6-4779-bf0a-0b9dafbd9ffa" class="r-7qj4rm alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Once you've made your purchase, simply email us at <a href="mailto:hi@withmonthlies.com">hi@withmonthlies.com</a> with your order number and request a consultation. Feel free to mention your preferred time slots and any specific concerns you'd like to address. Our team will be happy to hep schedule your session and provide the support you need.</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="178b7178-afd7-4a10-97a7-af8d32e055f0" class="r-1edzi8g" data-alchemy-prerendered-component-id="178b7178-afd7-4a10-97a7-af8d32e055f0">{%- comment -%}replo-liquid-chunk-begin{%- endcomment -%}<div style="width:100%;height:100%" data-alchemy-prerendered-placeholder="true">
